vendor/rupta contains the Rupta library source from the same revision.
Copyright (c) 2024 Wei Li. GNU GPL version 3. See LICENSE.
The port excludes the standalone launchers, compiler selection, memory monitor,
and upstream tests. Compiler API changes are made for the selected nightly.
The library port is in progress; production integration is not yet complete.
Production uses the imported PAG builder, call graph, call-site contexts,
delta propagator, and points-to sets for broad call discovery. The in-tree
flow analysis supplies context and state refinement. It feeds resolved calls
and typed callback and object-reference facts back to the backend. Shared
storage identities use Rupta address constraints and bidirectional MIR path
connections. These connections apply to new call contexts. The bridge merges
discovery contexts; the flow solver keeps precise state and context bindings.
The context-sensitive backend deduplicates complete argument and return
bindings separately from call-graph edges. A new binding for an existing edge
still adds its interprocedural constraints.
The port keeps generated instance identities and uses
the selected compiler for ABI checks. Legacy library shortcuts were replaced
with MIR analysis and narrow compiler-identified intrinsic models. The cast
constraint that can discard candidates is disabled by default. Raw-pointer
aggregates have data-pointer flow; unresolved vtable pairing and provenance
remain explicit coverage gaps. Full shared-memory integration remains open.

